<title>UK: British Steel dips after Usinor results.</title>
<headline>British Steel dips after Usinor results.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-09-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in British Steel Plc dipped on Tuesday in the wake of a cautious results statement from French steelmaker Usinor Sacilor, traders said.</p>
<p>The stock was down 1-1/4p at 190 by 0824 GMT.  </p>
<p>In Paris, Usinor shares were down 2.50 francs at 72.60.</p>
<p>Usinor said it expected second-half results to be weaker than the first half and posted a sharp drop in first-half net attributable profit to 833 million francs from 2.36 billion a year ago.</p>
<p>&quot;The poor results from Usinor have bit British Steel,&quot; said one trader.</p>
<p>-- David Holmes, London Newsroom +44 171 542 5106</p>
</text>
